Grouped prefill: extend assembled group state to the decode buffer's rows.

The adopted _assemble_groups_gdn_dev concatenates the per-group GDN states to
the active width and then copies that block into the persistent decode buffer,
which is allocated at the model's full batch capacity. ttnn.copy requires equal
logical shapes, so any active width below capacity fails during startup
warm-up:

  TT_FATAL: Input tensor shape Shape([4, 24, 128, 128]) does not match output
  tensor shape Shape([16, 24, 128, 128])

Grouping is therefore unusable whenever the service's decode buffer is wider
than the prefill width, which is the normal case (capacity 16, widths 1..8).

This patch extends the assembled block with a zero-filled device tail up to the
destination row count before the copy, for the recurrent state (batch rows on
dim 0) and for the convolution states (batch rows on dim 1). The tail is built
with ttnn.zeros plus ttnn.concat on the model's device, so no host round trip
and no pad-scalar ambiguity is involved.

Correctness of the zero tail: the only caller in this repository is
BatchedTracedDecodeAdapter.prefill_users, which calls reset_all() before
prefill, so every row is already zero when the tail is written. A source wider
than the buffer is refused rather than truncated, so a mistaken caller cannot
silently drop state.

--- a/models/demos/blackhole/qwen36/tt/model.py
+++ b/models/demos/blackhole/qwen36/tt/model.py
@@ -2929,10 +2929,42 @@
         (group g = users [g*group_size : ...])."""
         dn_layers = [layer.attention for layer in self.layers if not layer.is_full_attention]
         ng = len(group_rec_dev)
+
+        def fit_rows(tensor, target_rows, dim):
+            """Extend a batch dim up to the decode buffer's row count.
+
+            The decode buffer is allocated at the model's full batch capacity while the
+            assembled block spans only the active width, and ttnn.copy requires equal
+            logical shapes. The tail is zero-filled, which is safe because the only
+            caller (BatchedTracedDecodeAdapter.prefill_users) resets every row before
+            prefill. A source wider than the buffer is refused rather than truncated,
+            so no state can be dropped silently.
+            """
+            rows = int(tensor.shape[dim])
+            if rows == target_rows:
+                return tensor, None
+            if rows > target_rows:
+                raise ValueError(
+                    f"grouped state has {rows} rows above the {target_rows}-row decode buffer"
+                )
+            pad_shape = list(tensor.shape)
+            pad_shape[dim] = target_rows - rows
+            pad = ttnn.zeros(
+                tuple(pad_shape),
+                dtype=tensor.dtype,
+                layout=tensor.layout,
+                device=self.device,
+            )
+            return ttnn.concat([tensor, pad], dim=dim), pad
+
         for li, dn in enumerate(dn_layers):
             rec_full = ttnn.concat([group_rec_dev[g][li] for g in range(ng)], dim=0)  # [B, Nv, Dk, Dv]
             rec_src = rec_full if rec_full.dtype == dn.rec_state.dtype else ttnn.typecast(rec_full, dn.rec_state.dtype)
-            ttnn.copy(rec_src, dn.rec_state)
+            rec_fit, rec_pad = fit_rows(rec_src, int(dn.rec_state.shape[0]), 0)
+            ttnn.copy(rec_fit, dn.rec_state)
+            if rec_pad is not None:
+                ttnn.deallocate(rec_fit)
+                ttnn.deallocate(rec_pad)
             if rec_src is not rec_full:
                 ttnn.deallocate(rec_src)
             ttnn.deallocate(rec_full)
@@ -2940,7 +2972,11 @@
                 ttnn.deallocate(group_rec_dev[g][li])
             for m in range(dn.K):
                 conv_full = ttnn.concat([group_conv_dev[g][li][m] for g in range(ng)], dim=1)  # [1, B, D]
-                ttnn.copy(conv_full, dn.conv_states[m])
+                conv_fit, conv_pad = fit_rows(conv_full, int(dn.conv_states[m].shape[1]), 1)
+                ttnn.copy(conv_fit, dn.conv_states[m])
+                if conv_pad is not None:
+                    ttnn.deallocate(conv_fit)
+                    ttnn.deallocate(conv_pad)
                 ttnn.deallocate(conv_full)
                 for g in range(ng):
                     ttnn.deallocate(group_conv_dev[g][li][m])
